// Every mesh of the user's own showroom, from the compressed file.
//
// This is the check that matters, and the one that was missing: the cube has a
// single mesh, so it cannot tell a file-global address map from a per-ID one.
// The showroom has 29, all recording the same `dna_attributes` address, and it
// was silently giving all 29 the first mesh's geometry.
//
// The expected values come from a python reader implementing the same scoped
// rule, cross-checked against Blender's own reading of the file (29/29 meshes
// agree on vertex, polygon and loop counts and on the first vertex).
//
// The range check is the free self-check here: every index a triangle carries
// must be inside the vertex list it indexes. That is what 45% of triangles
// failed before, and it needs no reference at all to test.

t_all(string path) {
  t_all_open_report(path);
  t_all_count_report();
  t_range(path);
} return void;
